# Production-only overrides — Vite loads this automatically for `vite build`
# (mode=production, what Vercel runs), taking priority over the values in
# the shared .env. VITE_TILESERVER_URL points at a Docker container that
# only exists on a developer's own machine (docker-compose.yml's
# tileserver service) — in production it can never be reached, so every
# real visitor's browser spent ~1.5s per page load waiting for that health
# probe to time out and cancel before falling back to the public API
# (live-testing finding, 2026-08-03: two canceled "health" requests,
# ~1.5s each, visible in the Network tab). Empty here means
# selfHostedStyleUrl() skips the probe entirely — see MapView.vue's
# TILESERVER_URL/tileserverReachable comments. Set this to a real public
# tileserver URL once one exists (see docker-compose.yml's tile-builder/
# tileserver comments for that migration path).
VITE_TILESERVER_URL=
